+/*
+ * SWEET: MediaTek MTU3 (MT6983) USB device - CDC-ECM Ethernet and live log.
+ *
+ * matisse has a MediaTek MTU3 controller (mac@11201000, ippc@11203e00,
+ * SPI 160) rather than sweet's Qualcomm DWC3. LK leaves it powered, clocked
+ * and connected in high-speed device mode; this driver reuses those clocks
+ * and PHYs, resets only the device function (IPPC DEV_RST_CTRL bit 0), and
+ * brings the controller up for a CDC-ECM function. No GIC interrupt is used:
+ * EP0 and the QMU rings are polled from one kernel thread, like the UFS
+ * driver. Register names and the EP0/QMU state machines follow the vendor
+ * driver (drivers/usb/mtu3) for MT6983.
+ *
+ * Transport choices:
+ *  - EP0 is FIFO based (FIFO0): the data stage is copied by the CPU.
+ *  - Bulk IN/OUT and the notification IN use the QMU with gen2cp GPDs.
+ *  - The USB host and the controller are not cache coherent: the GPD rings
+ *    and data buffers are cleaned/invalidated around every hand-off.
+ *  - LK enabled 36-bit DMA (MISC_CTRL bit 31); GPD buffer and next-pointer
+ *    high nibbles are carried in bits 24:27 and 28:31 of dw0 (TX) or dw3
+ *    (RX), and the ring start high nibble in the QHIAR registers.
+ *
+ * Boot args: sweetusb=1 reports state only, sweetusb=2 (default for
+ * matisse) starts the device; sweetusblog=0 disables the UDP live log.
+ */
